  <item nodeId="node-15">
    <command xml:space="preserve">[enter]</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Most IF games are set in a world made up of rooms without internal division. Movement between rooms is possible; movement within a room does not always amount to anything. &gt;WALK OVER TO THE DESK is rarely a useful sort of command. On the other hand, if something is described as being high or out of reach, it is sometimes relevant to stand on an object to increase your height. This kind of activity tends to be important only if prompted by the game text.&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;Please press SPACE to continue.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-16"/>
    </children>
  </item>
